    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, im seeing this weird 500 error on our /api/v1/checkout endpoint sometimes. it happens randomly during peak traffic but i cant replicate it in staging. here is the log snippet from the last crash:\n\nError: Internal Server Error\nat RequestHandler (/app/src/middleware/auth.js:42:11)\nat processTicksAndRejections (node:internal/process/task_queues:95:5)\nUnhandledPromiseRejectionWarning: Timeout error connecting to redis_cache_cluster at 10.0.2.15:6379\n{ status: 500, code: 'ECONNRESET', detail: 'connection lost' }\n\nany idea what would cause this to be intermittent?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The intermittent behavior under peak traffic suggests a few likely culprits: your Redis cluster is probably hitting its max connection limit or timing out under load, which wouldn't happen in lower-traffic staging. The `ECONNRESET` combined with timeout points to connections being dropped—check if you're exhausting connection pooling, hitting Redis `maxclients`, or if there's a network/firewall idle timeout killing connections.\n\nAlso notable: your auth middleware is throwing an unhandled promise rejection (`processTicksAndRejections` in the stack). Even after Redis recovers, any fast or missing `try/catch` around the Redis call means one blip takes down requests. Add retry logic with exponential backoff on Redis timeouts and gracefully fall back (e.g., skip cache, still authenticate) so checkout doesn't 500 on cache hiccups.",
      "source": "target",
